    {
      "title": "Intel (INTC) — Buy/Hold/Sell Analysis",
      "type": "context",
      "content": "Intel has staged one of the most dramatic recoveries in large-cap semiconductor history, gaining +463.52% over the past year and +228.18% YTD to trade at $121.10. However, the stock has materially outrun both its fundamental valuation and its analyst price targets. The central tension in this analysis is a technically bullish chart colliding head-on with negative earnings, extreme forward multiples, and a consensus analyst target 23% below the current price. The question is not whether Intel has momentum — it clearly does — but whether that momentum is supported by underlying business fundamentals at this price level."
